so you have decided to play Amara or are  at least interested in playing Amara  well don't worry we have Jordan our  Amara expert here in the GameSpot office  Jordan we're gonna break down how Amaro  works how our skill trees work and what  are some best tips for Amara players  when playing through Borderlands 3 let's  start with her skill trees what are each  of her trees about okay so  Amara's three skill trees are fists of  the elements brawl and mystical assault  all of them are essentially just  different variations of getting Amara to  the middle of the fight as quickly as  possible because she does a lot of  damage at real close range so for  example the fist of the element skill  tree is about stopping the largest  threat so that you can deal with all the  smaller threats very quickly and then  focus on the big guy last whereas brawl  is about just jumping immediately into  the fight and mystical assault is kind  of to try to scatter enemies sig knock  them back on their feet and then you can  try to pick them off as they're trying  to recover okay  so what was the tree you went with what  do you find most useful for you at least  so I think that brawl is probably  Amara's best skill tree although I was  playing by my self for most of my time  with Borderlands 3 and brawl is kind of  her kind of self-sustaining skill tree  it's the one where she has the guardian  angel skill that allows her to just self  revive every two minutes so that's like  the skill tree you want to go into if  you're playing by yourself and you're  like I just need some defensive  abilities to make sure that I can  actually survive on my own but I also  really enjoyed investing in a few points  into her fist of the elements skill tree  which I think is probably the one that  you actually want to start with  especially if this is your first  Borderlands game or if you're just kind  of just getting into first-person  shooters and you just need a little bit  of assistance where are those specific  abilities he found useful  I would say in Fist of the elements in  her like very first tier she has a skill  called steady hands which increases her  weapon handling and accuracy so it just  makes it easier to actually hit your  target and just being able to use her  faze grasp ability to locked  one person in place just helps getting  those shots off so Borderlands 3 is  pretty hectic  lots of people running around this is  like the skill tree to kind of help you  stop all of that and try to get an  easier shot off to try to do as much  damage as possible it's also the tree  that if you invest five points into it  unlocks her second tier which unlocks  her perk which allows her to change her  active skill from doing shock damage to  fire damage in scenario damage and since  you mostly encounter bandits in the  beginning of Borderlands 3 being able to  do a lot of fire damage quickly and  effectively is probably the most useful  so you think maybe like invest in that  early on yeah I get that perk and then  maybe switch over to like a different  tree yeah exactly you have a few other  like second tier skills in there that  you could probably invest in a tempest  increases her elemental damage and  illuminated fist increases her melee  damage and allows her melee skill to  just incorporate whatever her active  skill element is so if you switch it  over to fire then all of her melee  attacks do fire damage which is just  very helpful in the beginning of the  game and then the last tree it seems  like you didn't really care for that one  as much yeah so mystical assault the  special action skill associated to this  one is called phase cast and phase cast  is when she like shoots out a projection  of herself which looks really cool and  does a lot of elemental damage but most  of the skills in this tree are designed  to increase the effectiveness of Amara's  action skills either she can use it more  often or it's just stronger and these  are all very good things but Amara is  already a very powerful character her  action skills are stupidly powerful like  I was able to by like the end of the  game just one-shot attacks with her  melee attacks I almost didn't even  actually have to use the guns in my  arsenal so using her action skill just  kind of made her almost too overpowered  but I can see how if you're playing with  multiple people and the enemies are kind  of stacked and becoming stronger this  might be the skill tree to invest in  points in  about halfway through the campaign when  enemies are a lot stronger and you might  just need that little bit of boost in  power and effectiveness okay so what  about weapons what what are Amara's  choice weapon types maybe brands that  you found useful for her so Mara has a  few skills like I said before that  increased her melee damage she also has  a few that just make her stronger the  closer she is to a person so close range  weapons are her bread-and-butter  close-range pistols shotguns assault  rifles that don't have really long range  scopes these are the things you want to  invest in I started with sniper rifles  for a while because I liked sniper  rifles and Borderlands games but it was  definitely clear about five hours and  that Amara's just not a sniper character  so it's kind of euro the person who  likes to go long range you're probably  better off picking one of the other  three as opposed to Amara well thank you  very much Jordan that is some pretty  good advice for Amara players sounds  like very much about shotguns getting  enclosed doing as much damage as  possible nope and if you are interested  in seeing how any of the other  characters play we have more guides for  all for Borderlands vault hunters on the  way you can also check out our witch  vault hunter is right for you video  which gives you a brief overview of each  character thanks for watching  [Music]
 

